RETRACTED LRC CONCLUSION — SEE MISTAKE-238.
The chi-zero terminal-descent claim below is false: THM-2075 transports
nonempty core safe sets, not the empty safe set of the full seam candidate.
The doubling identity, per-sheet homeomorphism, and numerical chi values survive.

========================================================================
P1  the DOUBLING IDENTITY  phi_{2C}(t) = phi_C(2t)  (the tower engine)
========================================================================
  ||(2c)t|| = ||c(2t)|| for all c  =>  phi_{2C}(t)=phi_C(2t) ? True
  => G_{2C}(delta) = D^{-1}(G_C(delta)): the safe set of 2C is the doubling-preimage of C's. The tower
     lifts a safe set through doubling; codex THM-2073's 'unique safe child' picks one preimage sheet.

========================================================================
P2  doubling as a CONTINUOUS BIJECTION: 2-to-1 on S^1, but a homeomorphism on each address half
========================================================================
  D:t->2t is 2-to-1 (preimages t/2 and t/2+1/2). The BINARY ADDRESS a in {0,1} (which half [0,1/2) or
  [1/2,1)) makes D|_[a/2,(a+1)/2) a homeomorphism onto S^1 (THM-2075 addresses). Verify the two preimages:
  s=0.3: D(t)=s at t=0.15 (addr 0) and t=0.65 (addr 1) ; 2*0.15=0.3, 2*0.65=0.30000000000000004
  s=0.7: D(t)=s at t=0.35 (addr 0) and t=0.85 (addr 1) ; 2*0.35=0.7, 2*0.85=0.7
  => the deck involution tau:t->t+1/2 swaps the two address sheets; on a single sheet D is a
     continuous bijection. (Distinct from my mirror iota:t->1-t, which is the reality/reversal Z/2.)

========================================================================
P3  chi-INVARIANCE (THM-2075) + MIRROR-PARITY (S212): chi even AND doubling-invariant
========================================================================
  S=[1, 2, 3, 4, 6] [2*{1,2,3} ∪ {1,3} odd]: chi(G_{1/14})=8 [EVEN]; has even speed (=> iota free => chi even, S212)? True
  S=[1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 12] [2*{1..6} ∪ {1,7}]: chi(G_{1/14})=24 [EVEN]; has even speed (=> iota free => chi even, S212)? True
  C=[1, 2, 3]: chi(G_C)=4, chi(G_{2C})=8  (G_{2C}=D^{-1}G_C: 2-to-1 preimage; ratio 8/4)
  C=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]: chi(G_C)=10, chi(G_{2C})=20  (G_{2C}=D^{-1}G_C: 2-to-1 preimage; ratio 20/10)
  => chi is EVEN for covering sets (mirror-parity) and tracked by the doubling map (THM-2075). A DISPROOF
